- A FRESH CUT COULD NOT BE GRABBED, FOR TWO REASONS AT ONCE (UI1, Robert: "cant grab normally grabers
  after split"). (1) A split happens AT the playhead, and the playhead's own 12 px grab strip sits
  above everything at z-index 4 — so it ate every press within 6 px of the boundary the split had
  just created. (2) The two handles that meet at that boundary — the END of the clip before and the
  START of the clip after — were both 12 px and centred on the same pixel, so the later one in the
  DOM won every press and dragging LEFT was unreachable. Cuts are z-index 5 now (the playhead is
  still draggable from anywhere along the lanes and the ruler; the cut is only grabbable at the cut),
  and a boundary too narrow to hold both handles splits its hit area down the middle: left half trims
  the clip that ends there, right half the clip that starts there, which is what the gesture already
  meant. Verified on prod: a left drag off a fresh split now opens the gap, which it could not do.
