  grabbers too, merge back"). It used to only extend the clip BEFORE the gap up to the one after it,
  leaving two spans touching at a point — and `normalizeSegments` merges OVERLAPS, never adjacencies,
  because a fresh split IS an adjacency and collapsing it would undo the split as it was made. So
  undo gave the material back and left a pair of boundary handles on an edge that cut nothing. It now
  splices the pair into one span; verified on prod (13 s take, cut to 11 s, undo → 0 handles, 0 gaps,
  13 s). THE ONE CASE THAT STILL DOES NOT MERGE is two clips at different SPEEDS (F5b) — merging
  throws one speed away — so there the boundary is real and keeps its handles. It does NOT ripple —
